1 NOTE * REMARKS:
2 CONT       Crusader 1099
2 CONT
2 CONT     * BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT       Hugues was born in 1057, the son of Henri I, king of France, andA
2 CONC nna of Kiev. He was the younger brother of King Philippe I. After 1067h
2 CONC e married Adelaide, comtesse de Vermandois et de Valois, only child ofH
2 CONC eribert IV, comte de Vermandois et de Valois and Adèle, comtesse deValo
2 CONC is. Hugues and Adelaide had five children of whom four would haveprogen
2 CONC y.
2 CONT
2 CONT       In early 1096 Hugues and Philippe began discussing the FirstCrusa
2 CONC de after news of the Council of Clermont reached them in Paris.Although P
2 CONC hilippe could not participate, as he had been excommunicated,Hugues was s
2 CONC aid to have been influenced to join the Crusade after aneclipse of the m
2 CONC oon on 11 February 1096.
2 CONT
2 CONT       That summer Hugues' army left France for Italy, where they wouldc
2 CONC ross the Adriatic Sea into territory of the Byzantine empire, unlikethe o
2 CONC ther Crusader armies which were travelling by land. On the way,many of t
2 CONC he soldiers led by fellow Crusader Emicho von Leiningen joinedHugues' a
2 CONC rmy after Emicho was defeated by the Hungarians, whose land hehad been p
2 CONC illaging. Hugues crossed the Adriatic from Bari in SouthernItaly, but m
2 CONC any of his ships were destroyed in a storm off the Byzantineport of Dyr
2 CONC rhachium.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Hugues and most of his army were rescued and escorted toConstanti
2 CONC nople, where they arrived in November 1096. Prior to hisarrival, Hugues s
2 CONC ent an arrogant, insulting letter to the Eastern RomanEmperor Alexius I C
2 CONC omnenos, according to the emperor's biography by hisdaughter (the _Alex
2 CONC iad_), demanding that Alexius meet with him.
2 CONT
2 CONT       'Know, O King, that I am King of Kings, and superior to all whoar
2 CONC e under the sky. You are now permitted to greet me, on my arrival, andt
2 CONC o receive me with magnificence, as befits my nobility.'
2 CONT
2 CONT       Alexius was already weary of the armies about to arrive, after th
2 CONC eunruly mob led by Peter the Hermit had passed through earlier in theye
2 CONC ar. Alexius kept Hugues in custody in a monastery until Hugues sworean o
2 CONC ath of vassalage to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT       After the Crusaders had successfully made their way across Seljuk
2 CONC territory and, in 1098, captured Antioch, Hugues was sent back toConsta
2 CONC ntinople to appeal for reinforcements from Alexius. Alexius wasunintere
2 CONC sted, however, and Hugues, instead of returning to Antioch tohelp plan t
2 CONC he siege of Jerusalem, went back to France. There he wasscorned for not h
2 CONC aving fulfilled his vow as a crusader to complete apilgrimage to Jerusa
2 CONC lem, and Pope Paschal II threatened to excommunicatehim. He joined the m
2 CONC inor Crusade of 1101, but was wounded in battle withthe Turks in Asia M
2 CONC inor about 5 September, and died of his wounds on 18October in Tarsus.
2 CONT
2 CONT       In 1103 his widow Adelaide married Renaud, comte deClermont-en-Be
2 CONC auvaisis, and they had two children. Adelaide died on 28September 1120 o
2 CONC r 1124.
