1 CHAN
2 DATE 11 MAY 2018
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Boleslaw was the second son of Wratislaw I, duke of Bohemia andDrahomir
2 CONC a von Stodar. Boleslaw was duke of Bohemia from 929 to hisdeath.
2 CONT
2 CONT Boleslaw is notorious for the murder, possibly at the behest of hismoth
2 CONC er Drahomira, of his brother Wenceslas (later canonised as St.Wenceslas
2 CONC ), the result of which brought him to the Czech ducal throne.Wenceslas w
2 CONC as murdered during a feast on 28 September 929, on the daywhen Boleslaw
2 CONC 's first son was born. He received the strange name ofStrachkwas, which m
2 CONC eant 'a dreadful feast'. Being remorseful for what hehad done, Boleslaw p
2 CONC romised to devote his son to religion and educatehim as a clergyman. He k
2 CONC ept his word.
2 CONT
2 CONT Despite the fratricide, Boleslaw is generally respected by Czechhistori
2 CONC ans as an energetic ruler. Citing Wenceslas' religious policiesas the c
2 CONC ause of Boleslaw's fratricide seems unlikely as Boleslaw in noway imped
2 CONC ed the growth of Christianity in Bohemia, and in fact heactually sent h
2 CONC is daughter Mlada, a nun, to Rome to ask permission tomake Prague a bis
2 CONC hopric.
2 CONT
2 CONT One major policy shift after the death of Wenceslas related toCzech-Ger
2 CONC man relations. It is usually asserted that Wenceslas was anobedient cli
2 CONC ent of the German King Heinrich 'the Fowler'. Boleslaw, onthe other han
2 CONC d, found himself almost immediately at war with Heinrich'ssuccessor Ott
2 CONC o 'the Great'. This conflict, presumably consisting ofborder raids (the g
2 CONC eneral pattern of warfare in this region at the time)between Boleslaw o
2 CONC n one side and the margrave of the Ostmark on theother, reached its con
2 CONC clusion in 950 when Boleslaw signed a peace withOtto. It cannot be said f
2 CONC or certain if Boleslaw became a vassal of theGerman king, but it is kno
2 CONC wn that he led a Czech force in alliance withOtto at the great victory o
2 CONC ver the Magyars at the Lech river (on 10August 955). He had also helped O
2 CONC tto to crush an uprising of Slavs onthe Lower Elbe in 953.
2 CONT
2 CONT Czech historians also claim that Boleslaw expanded his power intoSilesi
2 CONC a, Lusatia, and Moravia, but no dates are given for these allegedconque
2 CONC sts. If they did occur, they must have been only transitory gainsbecaus
2 CONC e Boleslaw's successors had to conquer them all over again.Boleslaw saw t
2 CONC he growth of Polish strength to the north of his bordersand he accordin
2 CONC gly arranged for his daughter Dobrawa to marry the Piastprince Mieszko I i
2 CONC n 965. Boleslaw died on 15 July 967 and was succeededby his son Bolesla
2 CONC w 'the Pious'.
