1 NOTE * BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT  Wratislaw was born about 888, the son of Borziwoy I, duke of Bohemia,a
2 CONC nd Ludmilla, heiress of Psov (later canonised, who is venerated as apat
2 CONC roness of Bohemia). He was the younger brother of Spitignew I, whosucce
2 CONC eded their father as duke of Bohemia. Spitignew is rememberedsolely for h
2 CONC is 895 alliance with Arnulf, duke of Bavaria (the Diet ofAugsburg). whi
2 CONC ch separated Bohemia from Great Moravia. Designed toprotect Bohemia aga
2 CONC inst the ravages of Magyar raiders, this pact alsoopened Bohemia to Eas
2 CONC t Frankish Carolingian culture and paved the wayfor the eventual triump
2 CONC h of Roman Catholicism in Czech spiritualaffairs. Spitignew died in 915 a
2 CONC nd was succeeded by Wratislaw.
2 CONT
2 CONT       About 906 Wratislaw married Drahomira von Stodar. They had threes
2 CONC ons and three daughters, of whom their son Boleslaw would have progeny.
2 CONC Wratislaw died in battle against the Magyars. His date of death isgener
2 CONC ally given as 13 February 921. He was succeeded by his 13-year-oldson W
2 CONC enceslas, who ruled Bohemia from the age of 18 but was murdered in935 b
2 CONC y a group of nobles allied with his younger brother Boleslaw.Wenceslas w
2 CONC as canonised, and remains the patron saint of the Czechpeople.
