1 NOTE He was about fifteen years old when, on 19 June 936 in Laon, he wascrow
2 CONC ned king. Late in 939 he married Gerberga of Saxony, the widow ofGiselb
2 CONC ert II of Lorraine, who then was anointed Queen of the Franks. InNovemb
2 CONC er 942 he lost Lorraine and part of Burgundy. On 13 July 945, atRouen, h
2 CONC e was captured by the Vikings who handed him over to Hugues theGreat. A
2 CONC fter he was released he settled, on 1 July 946, at Compiègne. Hewas abo
2 CONC ut thirty-four when he died, on 10 September 954 in Reims, aftera fall f
2 CONC rom his horse. His widow became regent for their son and, in959, Abbess o
2 CONC f Notre Dame in Soissons. She died in Reims on 5 May 984.
