1 NOTE When his father was killed in 972 he was a contender for the rule ofKie
2 CONC v, together with his elder two brothers. Yarapolk, the eldest brotheral
2 CONC ready established in Kiev, disposed of Oleg the other brother andforced V
2 CONC ladimir to flee the country. Vladimir went from Novgorod toScandinavia, f
2 CONC rom where he returned with an army of Varangians, attackedand killed Ya
2 CONC ropolk and in doing so became the sole ruler of Rus. In hisearly years a
2 CONC s a ruler he was brutal, bloodthirsty and dissolute. By hisfirst wife, R
2 CONC ogneda of Polotzk, he had four sons and two daughters; by aGreek woman h
2 CONC e fathered one son; by a Czech woman one son; two more sonsby a differe
2 CONC nt mother; and by a Bulgarian woman two more sons.Apparently he had thr
2 CONC ee hundred concubines at Vyshegorod, three hundredat Belgorod, and two h
2 CONC undred at Berestovo. He had married women broughtto him and as well def
2 CONC lowered virgins. At the beginning of his longreign he continued attacki
2 CONC ng the Byzantine Empire. However, he soonrealised that it was better to b
2 CONC e on good terms with his neighbours andadopted Christianity for himself a
2 CONC nd his people. This happened around988 when he also took as his third w
2 CONC ife the sister of the ByzantineEmperor. However, the Pechenegs continue
2 CONC d to harass him and he had tofight them continually until the end of hi
2 CONC s reign. After his conversionVladimir became a changed man; he became m
2 CONC ild towards criminals,generous to the poor and supported the Greek miss
2 CONC ionaries. This resultedin a picture of him that caused later generation
2 CONC s to look on St.Vladimir and his grandmother, St. Olga, as the first-bo
2 CONC rn of the newChristian people of Russia and her borderland. They were e
2 CONC steemed to besaints and Vladimir became the subject of a cycle of folkl
2 CONC ore and heroicpoems.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vladimir was a semi-barbaric Viking tribal chief of great leadershipabi
2 CONC lities; conquered and then was first ruler of a unified Russia; wasbapt
2 CONC ised at Kherson in the Crimea in 988 and 'converted' his subjects toChr
2 CONC istianity, and formed many alliances (many sealed with marriages ofhis c
2 CONC hildren) with the other leaders of Europe. His father sent him togovern N
2 CONC ovgorod in 970 despite his youth. He became Grand Duke, i.e.leader of h
2 CONC is people, by killing his brother Yaropolk, uniting Novgorodand Kiev. A
2 CONC fter becoming a Christian, Vladimir built churches, promotedcharity, es
2 CONC tablished Orthodox canon law and married Princess Anna,sister of Byzant
2 CONC ine Emperor Basil II and daughter of Romanus II (Emperor959-63) and his s
2 CONC econd wife Theophano. 'From the reign of Svyatoslav'syoungest son, Vlad
2 CONC imir, the Norman dynasty was definitely settled inKiev.' His feast day i
2 CONC s July 15th.
