1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Guillaume I-III, called 'Towhead' ('Tête d'étoupe') from the colour ofh
2 CONC is hair, was born in Poitiers about 900, the son of Ebalus Mancer,comte d
2 CONC e Poitou and Aremburgis. He claimed the duchy of Aquitaine on hisfather
2 CONC 's death, but the royal chancery did not recognise his ducal titleuntil t
2 CONC he year before his own death. He was 'count of the duchy ofAquitaine' f
2 CONC rom 959 and duke of Aquitaine from 962 to his death. He wasalso the cou
2 CONC nt of Poitou (as Guillaume I) from 935 and count of Auvergnefrom 950. T
2 CONC he primary sources for his reign are Ademar de Chabannes,Dudo of Saint-
2 CONC Quentin, and Guillaume of Jumièges.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 935 Guillaume married Gerloc of Normandy, daughter of Rollo, theViki
2 CONC ng leader to whom Charles 'the Simple' had given Normandy in 911.Rollo h
2 CONC ad died in 932. Guillaume and Gerloc (renamed Adele) had a sonand heir G
2 CONC uillaume who would have progeny.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after the death of King Raoul of France in 936, Guillaume wasco
2 CONC mpelled to forfeit some land to Hugues 'the Great', duke of TheFranks, c
2 CONC omte de Paris by Raoul's successor Louis IV 'd'Outremer'. Hedid it with g
2 CONC race, but his relationship with Hugues thenceforwarddeteriorated. In 95
2 CONC 0 Hugues was granted the duchies of Burgundy andAquitaine. He tried to c
2 CONC onquer Aquitaine with Louis' assistance, butGuillaume defeated them. Lo
2 CONC thar I, Louis' successor as king of France,feared the power of Guillaum
2 CONC e. In August 955 Lothar joined Hugues tobesiege Poitiers, which resiste
2 CONC d successfully. Guillaume, however, gavebattle and was routed.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Hugues in 956, his son Hugues Capet was named duke o
2 CONC fAquitaine, but he never tried to take up his fief, as Guillaume became
2 CONC reconciled with Lothar. Guillaume was given the abbey ofSaint-Hilaire-l
2 CONC e-Grand, which remained in his house after his death. Healso built a li
2 CONC brary in the palace of Poitiers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume retired to the abbey of Saint-Cyprien in Poitiers and left th
2 CONC egovernment to his son Guillaume II-IV. He died at Poitiers on 3 April9
2 CONC 63.
