1 NOTE His father died when he was only a child and it was his mother, theform
2 CONC idable Olga, who ruled Kiev until he was old enough to take charge.He t
2 CONC hen defeated the Khazars, the Ossetians and the Circassians but, in968 w
2 CONC hile he was away from Kiev, he almost lost his home base when itwas att
2 CONC acked by the Pechenegs. Having extended his territories into theBalkans
2 CONC , in 969 he was threatened by the Byzantines as they wanted himto withd
2 CONC raw. When he attacked the Empire he was defeated and the treatythat fol
2 CONC lowed forced him to return to Kiev. However, in 971 he returnedand this t
2 CONC ime was more successful, almost reaching Constantinople. TheEmperor bou
2 CONC ght him off with gifts and Svjatoslav also asked for gifts tobe given t
2 CONC o the families of the men who had died in the battles. Havingmade his p
2 CONC eace with the Emperor, he returned. However, the people ofPereyaslavets w
2 CONC arned the Pechenegs that Svjatoslav was on his way withonly a small com
2 CONC pany of men. Returning by boat, Svjatoslav approachedrapids and, as it w
2 CONC as not possible to pass through, he decided to winterthere. In the spri
2 CONC ng of 972 Svjatoslav again approached the rapids butthe Pechenegs, wait
2 CONC ing for him, and attacked and killed him. Taking hishead, made a cup of h
2 CONC is and, putting metal around the forehead, anddrank from it.
