1 NOTE On July 24 (July 11 old calendar), Orthodox Christians celebrate the da
2 CONC yof Saint Olga, the Grand Princess of Kiev.
2 CONT A legend says that Olga's fabulous beauty fascinated Prince Igor ofKiev
2 CONC . That's how Olga became the princess. The name and the birth placeof t
2 CONC he future enlightener of the Russian land was mentioned for thefirst ti
2 CONC me in the Russian Primary Chronicle, in the part that narratesabout Igo
2 CONC r's marriage: "and thou brought him wife from Pskov and Olgawas her nam
2 CONC e". The city of Pskov is now the center of Russia'snorth-western region
2 CONC .
2 CONT When her husband was killed by the hostile tribe of Drevlians, Olgabega
2 CONC n to rule the princedom on behalf of her juvenile son Svyatoslav.
2 CONT Grand Princess Olga went down to history as the creator of state andcul
2 CONC ture of Rus. She has done a lot to unite the lands of Russia and torein
2 CONC force the country.
2 CONT When already an adult, Olga was baptized in Constantinopolis andaccepte
2 CONC d the name of Helen. It was the emperor of Constantinopolis,Emperor Con
2 CONC stantine the Bagryanorodni , who became her godfather. InRussia Olga co
2 CONC mmenced erection of Christian temples and the preparationfor the conver
2 CONC sion of the Russian people to Orthodoxy. Saint Olga passedaway in 969.
2 CONT The baptizing of Rus took place in 988 during the reign of her grandson
2 CONC - Grand Prince Vladimir.
