1 NOTE FROM: Encyclopedia Britannica, www.britannica.com, Internet. Entry:Fran
2 CONC conia. Franconia German Franken,  one of the five great stem, orStamm (
2 CONC tribal), duchiesƒ_'the other four being Saxony, Lotharingia(Lorraine), S
2 CONC wabia, and Bavariaƒ_'of early medieval Germany. Today it isdivided betw
2 CONC een Rhenish Franconia, now located in the Lander (states) ofRhineland-P
2 CONC alatinate, Baden-WUrttemberg, and Hesse, and East Franconia,now in the L
2 CONC ander of Baden-WUrttemberg and Bavaria. The Franks forciblysettled the r
2 CONC egion from the early 6th century AD, and in the early 8thcentury the Me
2 CONC rovingian dynasty claimed it as a royal demesne (crownland). After the d
2 CONC ivision of the Carolingian empire under the Treaty ofVerdun in 843, Fra
2 CONC nconia became the nucleus of the East Frankish(German) kingdom, and, wh
2 CONC en the Carolingian line died out, Franconia'sduke became the first elec
2 CONC ted German king as Conrad I (911ƒ_'918). In919 the German crown passed t
2 CONC o a Saxon dynasty. Franconia remained aroyal demesne nurturing no stron
2 CONC g ducal dynasty, and their tenure of itprovided a support to German kin
2 CONC gs and Holy Roman emperors. By the 12thcentury, the name had come to re
2 CONC fer only to East Franconia.
