2 CONC c)1999, www.users.globalnet.co.uk\\_plk\\history.htm, Internet. PowysCe
2 CONC ntered around Shropshire at Caer Meguaidd, and covering much of themode
2 CONC rn Welsh border, Powys was Vortigern's native land. It seemsprobable th
2 CONC at in Vortigern's time Powys did not extend to the NorthWelsh coast, as t
2 CONC he king of Dogfeiling & Pengwern in the 7th centuryseems to have had ea
2 CONC sy access between his two kingdoms. Powys derivedits name from descript
2 CONC ive Latin (pagenses '(land of the) countrydwellers' or 'people of the p
2 CONC agi', the Roman equivalent of districtcouncil areas). Vortigern's secon
2 CONC d son was handed Powys when Vortigernbecame High King. In later years, a
2 CONC s the Norman attacks pushed in Wales'free borders, what was left of Pow
2 CONC ys came to be ruled by Gwynedd.
