1 NOTE FROM: Britannia Internet Magazine, www.britannia.com, Internet. St.Ursu
2 CONC la (born c.AD 305)(Welsh-Ursula, Latin-Ursula, English-Ursula)Though th
2 CONC ere are no ancient dedications to her in Britain, Ursula issaid to have b
2 CONC een a British Princess. After her father, 'King' Donaut,agreed to her m
2 CONC arriage with Governor Conan Meriadoc of Armorica(Brittany), she set sai
2 CONC l to join him along with 11,000 virginalhandmaidens. However, a miracul
2 CONC ous storm brought them over the sea in asingle day to a Gaulish port, w
2 CONC here Ursula declared that before hermarriage she would undertake a pan-
2 CONC European pilgrimage. Together, theBritish maidens headed for Rome where U
2 CONC rsula persuaded Pope Cyriacus andSulpicius, Bishop of Ravenna to join h
2 CONC er happy band of followers. Shewas later welcomed Pantulus, Bishop of B
2 CONC asle & Jaques, Bishop of Liege,and 'King' Ethereus arrived from Britain w
2 CONC ith Prince Conan himself.Together, they set out for Cologne which was b
2 CONC eing besieged by Huns. Ina dreadful massacre, the Huns beheaded all the v
2 CONC irgins and, with bow &arrow, their leader shot St. Ursula dead. Ursula a
2 CONC nd her virgins wereburied in Cologne where a great church is dedicated t
2 CONC o her. Conan, herhusband, apparently survived. Generally considered leg
2 CONC endary.
