1 NOTE FROM: http://www.tamworthcastle.freeserve.co.uk Tamworth Castle - TheGr
2 CONC eat Little English Castle 795-821 AD: Coenwulf, King of Mercia. 814AD: C
2 CONC oenwulf of Mercia signs two charters 'in vico celeberimmo quivocatur To
2 CONC moworthing'. Tamworth Castle is a Norman motte and baileycastle set in t
2 CONC he south-west corner of what was a Saxon burh, it'slocated to dominate t
2 CONC he approach over the two rivers which meet belowthe Castle. Its sandsto
2 CONC ne walls and superb herringbone wall - all thatsurvives of the 'curtain w
2 CONC all' of the bailey are believed to date fromthe 1180s. They replaced a p
2 CONC alisade and wooden tower, built on thepresent artificial mound shortly a
2 CONC fter the Norman Conquest of 1066.Numerous additions and alterations hav
2 CONC e been made to the castle bysucceeding generations of owners. Until in t
2 CONC he late 1890's, MarquisTownshend decided to sell the Castle by auction. T
2 CONC amworth Corporationpurchased it to mark Queen Victoria's Diamond Jubile
2 CONC e in 1897. Thepurchase price of Aœ3000 was later raised by public subsc
2 CONC ription and theCastle was formally opened and dedicated to the public t
2 CONC wo years later.
