1 NOTE FROM Britannia Internet Magazine, www.britannia.com, Internet. Arviragu
2 CONC sA personage who has come to our attention, first, in the writings ofJu
2 CONC venal, who mentions him in connection with resistance to Romanconquest a
2 CONC nd authority. Geoffrey of Monmouth refers to him as a Britishking whose b
2 CONC rother was killed sometime during Claudius' invasion (43AD). He has bee
2 CONC n linked with Caratacus, but more interestingly, he issaid by the inter
2 CONC polators of William of Malmesbury's 'De AntiquitateGlastoniensis Eccles
2 CONC iae' to be the king who granted 12 hides of landaround Glastonbury to J
2 CONC oseph of Arimathea  and his band of followers,when they brought Christi
2 CONC anity to Britain for the first time in 63 AD.Some scholars think that i
2 CONC t may have been Arviragus and his people whooccupied the ancient hillfo
2 CONC rt, located in the county of Somerset, knownas Cadbury Castle  (which w
2 CONC ould later come to be associated with KingArthur), and used it as a bas
2 CONC e for their resistance against the Romans.
