1 NOTE FROM: High McGough, Irish Kings, www.magoo.com/hugh/irishkings.html, Au
2 CONC g8, 2001, Internet. Eremon Alternate name forms: Heremon, Eremhom,Emhea
2 CONC r, EirireamhA3n, Eireamhon, h-Eremon Eremon was the seventh son ofMiles
2 CONC ius. Emher was his eldest brother. Joint rule in 3500. Eremhonkilled Em
2 CONC hear and his wife in 3500 in a quarrel over territory, andruled alone i
2 CONC nto 3516. During Eremon's reign alone, a '... colony calledby the Irish C
2 CONC ruithneaigh, in English 'Cruthneans' or Picts, arrived inIreland and re
2 CONC quested Heremon to assign them a part of the country tosettle in, which h
2 CONC e refused; but, giving them as wives the widows of theTuatha de-Danans, s
2 CONC lain in battle, he sent them with a strong party ofhis own forces to co
2 CONC nquer the country then called 'Alba,' but nowScotland; conditionally, t
2 CONC hat they and their posterity should betributary, to the Monarchs of Ire
2 CONC land.' Descendants of Milesius<http://www.hynes.net/milesius.html> on t
2 CONC he Hynes Clan web site. TaraMost of the Milesian kings ruled from Tara. '
2 CONC Tara is a prehistoricburial site in County Meath, famed as the legendar
2 CONC y capital of the highkings of Ireland, and a holy site for thousands of y
2 CONC ears. Here,according to tradition, elaborate rites were carried out bet
2 CONC ween thefuture high king of Tara and the goddess of sovereignty. Medb, f
2 CONC orexample, was said to have participated in a ritual union with nine of
2 CONC the high kings, preventing the rule of any candidates who refused tomat
2 CONC e with her. Another test was provided by the Stone of Fal, whichscreame
2 CONC d when it was touched by the rightful heir. There are claims thatCormac m
2 CONC ac Art, a leading figure in the Fionn cycle, established asumptuous cou
2 CONC rt at Tara and a lavish festival was also regularlycelebrated at Samhai
2 CONC n, on 1 November. 'In the fifth century, the placewas occupied by Niall o
2 CONC f the Nine Hostages and it was here that hispagan son, King Laoghaire, w
2 CONC as supposed to have been confronted by St.Patrick. After this, Tara's i
2 CONC mportance appears to have declined.' TheCeltic Connectionƒ_'Tara<http:/
2 CONC /www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/Marina/4870/celtic.html>.
2 CONT
