2 CONC ach-Teamrach, Aonghus III (Tuirmheach), Aongus (or A+neas)Tuirmeach-Tea
2 CONC mrach, Angus Tuirbheach; Aonghusa turmigh m Echachfoiltletain m Oilella c
2 CONC aisfhiaclaigh m Connla cruaidcelgaigh (O'Clery<oclery.html>) Died at Te
2 CONC amhair. One source says he was murdered. 'Hisson, Fiacha Firmara (so ca
2 CONC lled from being exposed in a small boat on thesea).' Aenghus was ancest
2 CONC or of the Kings of Dalriada, and Argyle inScotland.' Descendants of Mil
2 CONC esius <http://www.hynes.net/milesius.html>on the Hynes Clan web site. A
2 CONC enghus, under the name of Angus Turbech ofTara, is the First king of Da
2 CONC l Riada listed in the Book of Ballymote<http://www.magma.ca/~mmackay/da
2 CONC lriada.html>. See my table of ScotsKings <www.magoo.com\\hugh\\scotskin
2 CONC gs.html>, #53 in the table of thekings of Dal Riada.
