2 NOTE This obituary was taken from the Casket, Antigonish, N.S.  "At the home
3 CONC of her daughter, Mrs. E. Corbett, Levis, P.Q. March 12, 1928, of heartf
3 CONC ailure Mrs. Mary E. MacDonald, Lourdes, N.S. Deceased was born atArisai
3 CONC g, August 3, 1859, a daughter of the late Donald G. Ross andMargaret Gi
3 CONC llis. Prepared by the last rites of Holy Mother Church,conscious to the l
3 CONC ast moment and knowing full well that death was near,her only wish was t
3 CONC hat God would spare her until her family--Mrs. T. A.O'Sullivan, Jonquie
3 CONC re, Que., Miss Eunice, of New York, Dan P. and W. B.,of Lourdes and Rod
3 CONC erick, of Detroit, hastily summoned by telegraph andspeeding to her bed
3 CONC side would reach her before she passed away. Butdeath won out and they h
3 CONC ad the sad duty of accompanying their mother'sremains to her former hom
3 CONC e at Lourdes. The funeral was held on Fridaymorning, March 16 and was l
3 CONC argely attended. The remains were taken toOur Lady of Lourdes Church, w
3 CONC here mass was elebrated by Rev. FatherMacLellan after which they were c
3 CONC onveyed to Lourdes Cemetery and laid torest beside those of her much be
