2 TYPE Anecdote
2 NOTE came to Evanston IL with his parents, the Rev. & Mrs. Charles Bragdon, a
3 CONC sa boy of nine, and after attending the grammar school he graduated fro
3 CONC mNorthwestern University in 1870.  Soon after graduation, he pursued hi
3 CONC sstudies at the Chicago Medical College and in Vienna, and at HahnemonM
3 CONC edical School in Philadelphia.  He also received special surgicaltraini
3 CONC ng in Vienna, Austria.  He then returned to Evanston and beganpractice t
3 CONC here in 1873. in 1891 he conceived the idea of starting ahospital in Ev
3 CONC anston and it was due to a suggestion of his that theEvanston Emergency H
3 CONC ospital was founded. Two of his patients, Mrs.Butler and Mrs. Kidder, u
3 CONC ndertook the organization. From it has grownthe present Evanston Hospit
3 CONC al, one of the best-equipped and best-managedin the country, on whose s
3 CONC taff Dr. Bragdon served continuously for 35years. He took an active int
3 CONC erest in public affairs, and was one of thefounders and original stockh
3 CONC olders of the State Bank of Evanston, laterthe State Bank and Trust Com
3 CONC pany, and now the State National Bank. Hewas also a member of its Board o
3 CONC f Directors. He was a member of Phi BetaKappa, honourary scholastic fra
3 CONC ternity; the Evanston Club; the CountryClub of Evanston; and the Chicag
3 CONC o Homeopathic Society. He was keenlyactive for the best interests of No
3 CONC rthwestern University, from whichinstitution he and his four children a
3 CONC ll graduated (all Phi Beta Kappa).Dr. and Mrs. Bragdon were married at t
3 CONC he Philadelphia CentennialExposition in 1876 and celebrated their golde
3 CONC n wedding anniversary in1926.
