1 WILL
2 DATE 19 OCT 1659
2 NOTE Will of Isaac Allerton
3 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------
3 CONC ---------
3 CONT
3 CONT At a Court of Magistrates Octob. 19. 59
3 CONT A writeing presented as the last will & Testament of Isaac Alerton, lat
3 CONC eof Newhaven deceased, wth an account of certaine debts, dew to him; &f
3 CONC rom him;
3 CONT An account of Debts at the Duch
3 CONT first, 700. & odd gilders from Tho: Hall by Arbitration of CaptaineWill
3 CONC et, & Augustine Harman; about Captaine Scarlet wch I paid out,
3 CONT And there is 900 gilders owing by John Peterson the Bore, as by GeorgWo
3 CONC olseyes booke will appeare; & severall obligations thereto,
3 CONT ffrom Richard Cloufe owes, as Georg Woolseyes Booke will make appeare; I
3 CONC thinke 900. gilders, but his Estate being broken. I Desire that what ma
3 CONC ybe gotten may be layd hold on for mee,
3 CONT Due from william Goulder 270, od gilders, by his Bill appeares;
3 CONT Due from John Snedecare a shoomaker 150, od gilders as by his accoappea
3 CONC res.
3 CONT from the widdow of the Hanc Hancson due as by severall Bills & accounts
3 CONC ;
3 CONT Peter Cornelioussen 120. od guilders as by ye account will appeare.
3 CONT Due from Henry Brasser for rent for 28 moneths, from the first October1
3 CONC 656. to the last of May 58: for three roomes at 3 gilders a week. I ami
3 CONC n his Debt for worke of the old acco wch must be Deducted;
3 CONT 156 Isaac Allerton's Will and Inventory.
3 CONT there is 20 li in George Woolseyes hand, that came fro. mr Tho Maybuefo
3 CONC r mee
3 CONT There is 420. oaf. gilders that I owe to Nicholas, the ffrenchman, & aC
3 CONC ooper I owe something to, wch I would have that 201; in Georg Woolseyes
3 CONC hand, & the rest of that in Henry Brassers hand to them two;
3 CONT And now I leave my son Isaac Allerton and my wife, as Trustees toreceiv
3 CONC e in my debts, & to pay what I owe, as farr as it will goe & whatis ove
3 CONC rpluss I leave to my wife and my sonne Isaac, as far as theyreceive the D
3 CONC ebts to pay what I owe;
3 CONT In Captaine Willetts hand. a pcell of booke lace 1300 & odd. guildersWc
3 CONC h I left in trust with Captaine Willett to take care of: Seale
3 CONT My brother Bruster owes mee foure score pounds & odd. as the obligation
3 CONC swill appeare.
3 CONT Besides all my Debts in Delloware Bay & in Virgenia wch in my booke wil
3 CONC lappeare, & in Barbadoes. what can be gott; Witness. Isaac AllertonSeni
3 CONC or John Harriman
