2 NOTE When he was ten years old in 1798, the British entered Enniscorthy. His
3 CONC mother was already dead. His Grandmother, who was still quite young att
3 CONC he time, put flour in her hair, which was still black, to made it lookw
3 CONC hite, and put him on her back. She told James that if the soldiersasked h
3 CONC im any questions to say:'This is my grandmother and she speaksIrish'.  S
3 CONC he said to him: 'I am not asking you to tell any lies, becauseI do spea
3 CONC k Irish.' When the soldiers were going past them, he cried out:'This is m
3 CONC y grandmother and she speaks Irish.' The soldiers let them go.She was b
3 CONC ent over and her hair was grey.
