2 DATE 8 JAN 1899
2 PLAC Arisaig, Antigonish Co., Nova Scotia, Canada
2 NOTE Sudden Death.--Mr Donald Ross, an aged and greatly respected farmer ofA
3 CONC risaig, died suddenly on Sunday. He appeared to be in his usual healthS
3 CONC unday morning, having attended Mass, and afterwards visited the Glebeho
3 CONC use, where he remained until about four o'clock. On his way home hecall
3 CONC ed at the house of Mr. Gillis, which is situated but a shortdistance fr
3 CONC om the Glebe. While in the act of greeting the inmates, hefell to the f
3 CONC loor and became speechless. Fr. McDonald was immediatelysummoned and ad
3 CONC ministered the last sacraments to the dying man, who didnot regain cons
3 CONC ciousness. The cause of death was no doubt heart trouble.Mr. Ross was a m
3 CONC ost highly esteemed man and great sorrow is felt for hissudden death. I
3 CONC t was his son, Andrew, who with his wife, was drowned onthe coast of Al
3 CONC aska last Spring. R.I.P. (age 68)
