2 DATE 19 MAR 1926
2 PLAC Arisaig, Antigonish Co., Nova Scotia, Canada
2 NOTE I have been told that Margaret enjoyed smoking her pipe. At. Arisaig, N
3 CONC .S. on Friday, March 19, 1926, Margaret relict of Donald Ross anddaught
3 CONC er of Alexander Gillis, Alasdair Maclain bhan, at the venerableage of 9
3 CONC 3 years. In her last illness, she was often fortified by thesacraments o
3 CONC f Holy Church, and was accorded the rare favor of dying onthe Feast of S
3 CONC aint Joseph, the glorious patron of a happy death. And herlive was exem
3 CONC plary as her death was happy. Of her family of tenchildren, seven survi
3 CONC ve, namely John, Arisaig; William J., Antigonish;Ronald, Newton, Mass.; M
3 CONC rs John C. MacDonald, Vancouver, B. C.; Mrs AlexJ. MacDonald, Maryvale, N
3 CONC . S. ; Mrs. Alex A. MacDonald, and Mrs. RonaldMcInnis, Lourdes, N. S. H
3 CONC er funeral was largely attended. The requiemmass was celebrated by Rev. J
3 CONC . J. MacKinnon, a nephew of the deceased,and Father Rankin, the pastor, o
3 CONC fficiated at the grave. Eternal restgrant to her, O Lord. and let light p
3 CONC erpetual shine upon her.
