2 NOTE Death Notice 1949, from the Casket, Antigonish, Nova Scotia, Canada
3 CONT Mrs. Clarence C. Allbee, Yonkers, New York, Former Hospital Supervisor
3 CONT
3 CONT "Mrs Eunice MacDonald Allbee, a registered nurse and onetime supervisor
3 CONC of the nursing staff at St. Joseph's Hospital, died last night in herho
3 CONC me at 18 Coyle Place after a long illness. She was the wife ofClarence C
3 CONC . Allbee of the composing room staff of The Herald Statesman.Born in Lo
3 CONC urdes, N.S., Canada, Mrs. Allbee came to the United States in1921 to en
3 CONC ter nurses training school of St. Joseph's Hosp. in Yonkers.After her g
3 CONC raduation she served there for a time as supervisor of thenursing staff a
3 CONC nd later went into private practice. She was married hereto Mr. Allbee o
3 CONC n Sept 1, 1929 and practiced little
3 CONT after that. In W.W. II, however, Mrs. Allbee returned to St. Joseph'sHo
3 CONC sp. to give her services voluntarily. She was a Communicant of theChurc
3 CONC h of St. Denis. Surviving Mrs. Allbee besides her husband are asister, M
3 CONC rs. Thomas J. O'Sullivan of New Glascow, N. S., three brothers,Dan P. M
3 CONC acDonald, New Glascow, William B., Lourdes and Roderick J. ofDetroit, M
3 CONC ichigan and several nieces and nephews.
