2 DATE 1639
2 NOTE In 1639 Henry removed with Rev. Lothrops to Barnstable where he settled
3 CONC permanently. He was a deacon 44 years, and ordained Elder in 1670.Serve
3 CONC d as Deputy in the Plymouth Court or Legislature for 7 years. Was ausef
3 CONC ul and valuable man. Died in 1679, when he was about 83 years old.The d
3 CONC escendants of Henry Cobb are very numerous and are at the presenttime v
3 CONC ery widely scattered. They were of the true Pilgrim stock and ithas alw
3 CONC ays been a deeply religious family, numbering many Ministers andDeacons a
3 CONC mong its members, and as a class have been noted for theirloyalty to th
3 CONC e church.
