1 WILL
2 DATE 23 AUG 1763
2 NOTE In the name of God, amen.
3 CONT On the 23rd day of August 1763 I Samuel Cushman of Attleboro in theCoun
3 CONC ty of Bristol in the Province of the Massachussetts Bay in the NewEngla
3 CONC nd, yeoman, being of perfect mind and memory, blessed be God for itand c
3 CONC alling all men once to die do make this my last will and testamentand p
3 CONC rincipally and first of all give and recomend my soul to the Handsof Go
3 CONC d who gave it and my body I recommend to the earth to be buried ina dec
3 CONC ent christian burial at the discretion of my executor after namednothin
3 CONC g doubting but that the general resurection of ye body I shallreceive y
3 CONC e same again by ye mighty power of God and as touching allwordly goods o
3 CONC r estate wherewith it hath pleased God to bless me in thislife and worl
3 CONC d I give and dispose of in  the following manner and form.
3 CONT I give to Fear my dearly beloved wife a fire-room in my house where she
3 CONC shall choose to dwell in also what room in ye chamber and cellar shesha
3 CONC ll need. Likewise I give to my wife ye use of all my household goodswit
3 CONC hin doors further my will is that my two daughters Desire Foster andMer
3 CONC cy Fuller shall have all my household goods which remain after mywife F
3 CONC ear decease (the hatchel only excepted)
