2 TYPE Misc
2 NOTE 'French Canadian and Acadian Genealogical Review', Spring 1968. Page16-
3 CONC 26. He signed his name as 'Guion', and it is from him that Guyon, andma
3 CONC ny Dion and Dionnes descend. His godfathers are Jean Collin and PierreD
3 CONC olivet, and godmother Catherine Goddin. He grew up in Tourouvre, on May
3 CONC 18, 1614, he signed at loan to Pantaleon Bigot, a farmer from Autheuil,
3 CONC a sum consisting of: 'a small gold pistol, pieces of fifty-two sons,qua
3 CONC rters of crowns and other silver pieces'. For a value of about 84pounds
3 CONC . He was already a mason although only 24 years of age, was verysuccess
3 CONC ful. Jean built the old stairs of the steeple tower of the churchat Tou
3 CONC rouvre in 1615. He was then living in the parish of St-Jean deMortagne, p
3 CONC rovince of Perche, France.
