2 NOTE Edward Fuller was the son of Robert and Sara (Dunkhorn) Fuller ofRedenh
3 CONC all, Norfolk, England.  Some accounts give his mother as Francis,but Fr
3 CONC ancis appears to be Robert Fuller's second wife.  Robert's firstwife Sa
3 CONC ra was buried 1 July 1584, and thus would have been the mother ofEdward F
3 CONC uller. Edward Fuller's brother Samuel Fuller also came toAmerica on the M
3 CONC ayflower.  Edward Fuller married, and moved to Leyden,Holland for a sho
3 CONC rt time before coming to America.  The name of his wifeis not known.  J
3 CONC ames Savage, in his "Genealogical Dictionary of theFirst Settlers of Ne
3 CONC w England" says Edward Fuller's wife was named Ann.However, this appear
3 CONC s to have simply been a typographical error.Samuel and Edward Fuller we
3 CONC re one set of brothers to come on theMayflower, but another set of brot
3 CONC hers were John and Edward Tilley.Edward Tilley had a wife named Ann, no
3 CONC t Edward Fuller. BIOGRAPHICALSUMMARY:
3 CONT Edward Fuller, his wife, and his son Samuel came to America on theMayfl
3 CONC ower.  They had lived in Leyden, Holland for a short period oftime, but o
3 CONC riginally came from Redenhall, Norfolk, England.  EdwardFuller's father w
3 CONC as a butcher by trade, and his brother Samuel was adoctor and deacon.  E
3 CONC dward's occupation, however, remains unknown.  Heand his wife both died t
3 CONC he first winter.
