1 EVEN
2 TYPE Anecdote
2 NOTE Angus Pioneer MacDonald
3 CONT Letters in Halifax Chronicle from Aonghas Qg (Young Angus), reprinted i
3 CONC nAntigonish Casket. Letters deal with Father D.J. Rankin (History ofCou
3 CONC nty of Antigonish) statement that Angus Gillis took the MacDonaldname t
3 CONC o get Glenaladale's help to get land in Merigomish.
3 CONT Casket July 31, 1924
3 CONT Angus Gillis was adopted by his near relative MacDonald of Glenaladalew
3 CONC hen a child in Scotland, so was made a member of the Laird's ownfamily. I
3 CONC n his teens he came to Prince Edward Island with Glenaladale.Glenaladal
3 CONC e had 20,000 acres in P.E.I. but never secured a foot of landin Nova Sc
3 CONC otia for himself or anyone else.
3 CONT Young Angus MacDonald joined Glenaladale's Regiment during the American
3 CONC Revolution. On disbandment in 1784 he got a soldier's grant of land nea
3 CONC rthe mouth of (illegible, likely Sutherland's River]. Hence he -was kno
3 CONC wnto his contemporaries as Aonghas na h'aibhne -- Angus at the River. S
3 CONC omeyears later he bought a lot of 400 acres at Merigomish about 2 miles
3 CONC from his first settlement. There some of his descendants are to be foun
3 CONC dtoday. He bought this land from Sir John Wentworth on October 25, 1815
3 CONC for the sum of 400 pounds sterling. It was registered at Pictou onNovem
3 CONC ber 10, 1815 on the oathe of William Fraser before Hugh Denoon,Deputy R
3 CONC egistrar.
3 CONT Casket August 3, 1924
3 CONT Father Rankin questions Aonghas Og sources and credibility.
3 CONT Casket August 28, 1924
3 CONT Aonghag Og demolishes Rankin.
