2 NOTE The home of this family of the MacLeods was in a pretty place calledCli
3 CONC adal on the west side of Eigg. The MacLeods of Cliadal were theoldest f
3 CONC amily in Eigg, for they were the only family that escapeddestruction at t
3 CONC he time the Clanranald MacDonalds weresmothered to deathin Uamha Raing b
3 CONC y the MacLeods. A sister of the chief of the MacLeodswas married to Cla
3 CONC nranald. The old people speak of her as the "beautifulwoman" but she wa
3 CONC s mistreated by her husband. Some indignity offered tohis people by the M
3 CONC acDonalds in Eigg added fuel to the flame, andMacLeod sent a force to p
3 CONC unish the MacDonalds of Eigg who, forwarned,took refuge in a large cave n
3 CONC ear the shore. Unfortunately, theirpresence was discovered and the MacL
3 CONC eods, unable to enter, piled up amass of combustible matter before the e
3 CONC ntrance, and setting it on fire,smothere the helpless MacDonalds to dea
3 CONC th. The MacLeods of Cliadal tookrefuge in another cave and thus escaped t
3 CONC he catastrophe that cut off therest of the natives.
