2 NOTE "JOHN JAMES ROSS The Gulf Shore lost a staunch citizen in the death ath
3 CONC is Arisaig home June 13th of John James Ross, aged 86, following threew
3 CONC eeks illness. Son of the late Donald and Margaret (Gillis) Ross, he was
3 CONC born at Pleasant Valley, and moved with his parents to Arisaig when ani
3 CONC nfant. Mr. Ross became a key-man in the community life of Arisaigparish
3 CONC . Neighbors and others sought his wise counsel and readyassistance in t
3 CONC imes of perplexity and trouble. He was a kindly man whoenjoyed helping o
3 CONC thers and seeing people prospering and happy. Goodfortune to neighbors b
3 CONC rought gladness to his great heart. As asuccessful farmer and fisherman h
3 CONC e understood freely the successes anddisappointments of the North Shore p
3 CONC eople. St. Margaret's church, inparticular, will miss his sincere and l
3 CONC oyal support, for Mr. Ross wasits warden for nearly forty years. He was m
3 CONC arried twice, the first wife,Margaret MacDougall, Arisaig, predeasing h
3 CONC im by 47 years. Survivingchildren are a son Dan, and a daughter, Christ
3 CONC y, Mrs. Herman Paterson,Roxbury, Mass. The second Mrs. Ross, his widow, w
3 CONC as the former SarahMacDonald, daughter of Alexander MacDonald, McArra's B
3 CONC rook, and Mary(Grant) MacDonald, Knoydart. There are four children surv
3 CONC iving from thisunion: Andrew, California; Alexander, Arisaig; John, R.C
3 CONC .A.F.; Margaret,Mrs. Charles Oliver, Brighton, Mass. A brother, W. J. R
3 CONC oss, Antigonish:a sister Mrs. Alexander MacDonald, Brighton, Mass, and 1
3 CONC 3 grandchildrenalso survive. The funeral was largely attended. Solemn r
3 CONC equiem Mass inSt. Margaret's Church was celebrated by Rev. D.C. MacEach
3 CONC ern.P.P.,assisted by Rev. C.F. Ross as deacon, and Rev. A. Ross, sub-de
3 CONC acon,cousins of the deceased, and Rev. Neil MacKenzie, master of ceremo
3 CONC nies.Pall bearers were Allan R. MacDonald, Donald MacDonald, AndrewMacD
3 CONC onald, C. D. Gillis, Archibald MacInnis, Hugh D. MacDonald and DanJ. Ma
3 CONC cDonald. R.I.P.
3 CONT CARD OF THANKS Mrs. J.J.Ross and family wish to convey their gratefulth
3 CONC anks to all who sent Mass Cards and flowers and who in any other wayexp
3 CONC ressed sympathy and tendered assistance during thier recentbereavement; t
3 CONC hey are particularly grateful to their pastor, Rev. D.MacEachern, Rev. A
3 CONC . Ross, Boisdale, Rev. F. Ross, Maryvale and Rev. NeilA. MacKenzie,."
