1 NOTE Philippe II, king of France, widower of Isabelle of Flanders, wanted to
2 CONC make friends with the king of Denmark by marrying his  daugther,Ingebor
2 CONC g. But the Danes were then very backward in culture and learningand poo
2 CONC r Ingeborg was a dull, ignorant girl, not at all like a courtlylady.    P
2 CONC hilippe took such a dislike to her that he sent her into aconvent and i
2 CONC nstead married the beautiful Agnès of Meran. Pope  InnocentIII espoused t
2 CONC he cause of Ingeborg and eventually put the kingdom underan interdict. H
2 CONC e threatened to forbid any service to go on in any churchexcept in thos
2 CONC e of the monks and nuns, and there only with the doorsshut against all o
2 CONC utsiders. The whole nation was going to be cut offfrom God because of t
2 CONC he monarch's sin.  Philippe pretended to agree to aseparation from Agne
2 CONC s. In fact, he did not turn her away and Ingeborgwas imprisoned. Agnes d
2 CONC ied in 1201, and her children by Philippe werelegitimised by the Pope.
