1 NOTE was of very small stature and very little is known about her early year
2 CONC s.Being a descendant of the English King Alfred The Great was one reaso
2 CONC nwhy William, Duke of Normandy, sought her in marriage. Apparently sher
2 CONC efused him as she did not want to be married to a bastard. Furious,Will
2 CONC iam forced entry to her room and gave her a beating. However, thisrathe
2 CONC r unconventional behaviour resulted in her changing her mind andthey ma
2 CONC rried in 1051, although they had to wait until 1059 before thepapal dis
2 CONC pensation arrived. William relied heavily on her and she actedas regent i
2 CONC n Normandy whenever he was absent. After the conquest ofEngland, she wa
2 CONC s crowned William The Conqueror's queen at Winchester.She went to the n
2 CONC orth of England with him and at Selby gave birth to thefuture King Henr
2 CONC y I, probably their tenth or eleventh child. In the year1069 she went b
2 CONC ack to the Duchy of Normandy where she remained incharge. When she beca
2 CONC me ill in 1083, William The Conqueror hurried overfrom England to be wi
2 CONC th her. However, she died on 2 November 1083 atCaen and was buried ther
2 CONC e.
