2 CONC ise, she was married to the sixty-one year old Aethelwulf, King ofWesse
2 CONC x. However, he died on 13 January 858 and in that year she marriedhis s
2 CONC on, Aethelbald, but this marriage was annulled. After her secondhusband d
2 CONC ied in 860, she returned to France only to have her father keepher impr
2 CONC isoned in Senlis. However, about Christmas 861 she eloped toLorraine wi
2 CONC th Baudouin I, Count of Flanders, who lost his county becauseof this, e
2 CONC arly in 862 they married and when the pope reconciled themwith her fath
2 CONC er, Emperor Charles the Bald, the latter then returnedFlanders to Baudo
2 CONC uin.
