1 NOTE The area now known as Holland was formerly known as Friesland, orWest-F
2 CONC riesland, and its first counts were entitled Count of Friesland.At that t
2 CONC ime, Friesland covered the area from the mouth of the riverWeser (near G
2 CONC ermany's Bremen) to nearly inside modern Belgium. Todaythis area is div
2 CONC ided into five provinces: Zeeland, South-Holland,North-Holland, Friesla
2 CONC nd and Groningen. However, the area ruled over bythese counts was only a v
2 CONC ery small section of the total. From when thefirst known count lived ar
2 CONC ound the year 889, it took until 1100 beforehis descendants became know
2 CONC n as Counts of Holland. Apparently the nameHolland was derived from the w
2 CONC ord 'Holtland', which meant either 'Landwith a hollow' or 'wood (hout/h
2 CONC olt) land'. In 922, Count Dirk I received(from Charles The Simple, King o
2 CONC f the West-Franks, or France) the churchin Egmond and its estates which b
2 CONC ecame the centre of his county. In 925,while formally belonging to the L
2 CONC orraine area, Holland became part ofthe Holy Roman Empire. However, the C
2 CONC ount and his subjects preferred tothink themselves independent of any o
2 CONC verlord; accordingly they madetheir own alliances as they saw fit.
