1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Ragenold/Renaud was probably the son of another Renaud, who was namedfr
2 CONC om 924 to 941 in Anjou, and who was perhaps count of Soissons. Theearli
2 CONC er Renaud could have been a nephew of Foulques I, comte d'Anjou(870-938
2 CONC ). About 945 Ragenold married Alverade de Lorraine, daughter ofGiselber
2 CONC t, duke of Lorraine and Gerberga von Sachsen, daughter of theEmperor-El
2 CONC ect, Heinrich I 'the Fowler'. Ragenold and Alverade had a sonGiselbert a
2 CONC nd daughter Ermentrud/Irmgard who would have progeny.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 948 Ragenold was acknowledged as count of Roucy. In the same year he
2 CONC rebuilt the château de Roucy, and he was excommunicated by the Church.H
2 CONC e died on 10 May 967 and was buried in the abbey of St. Remi in Reims.
