1 NOTE Henry of Scotland (Eanric mac Dabíd, 1114 – 12 June 1152) was a Prince o
2 CONC fScotland, heir to the Kingdom of Alba. He was also Earl ofNorthumberla
2 CONC nd and Earl of the Honour of Huntingdon and Northampton.
2 CONT He was the son of King David I of Scotland and Maud, 2nd Countess ofHun
2 CONC tingdon. His maternal grandparents were Waltheof, Earl of Northumbriaan
2 CONC d Huntingdon, (beheaded 1075) and his spouse Judith of Lens.
2 CONT Henry was named after his uncle, King Henry I of England who had marrie
2 CONC dhis paternal aunt Edith of Scotland (the name Edith gallicised asMatil
2 CONC da after becoming Queen consort in 1100). He had three sons, two ofwhom b
2 CONC ecame King of Scotland, and a third whose descendants were toprove crit
2 CONC ical in the later days of the Scottish royal house. He alsohad three da
2 CONC ughters.
2 CONT His eldest son became King of Scots as Malcolm IV in 1153. Henry'ssecon
2 CONC d son became king in 1165 on the death of his brother, reigning asWilli
2 CONC am I. Both in their turn inherited the title of Earl of Huntingdon.His t
2 CONC hird son, David also became Earl of Huntingdon. It is from the 8thEarl t
2 CONC hat all Kings of Scotland after Margaret, Maid of Norway claimdescent.
