1 NOTE He was the Earl of Surrey. Kin of Mellcene Thurman SmithGenealogyLibrar
2 CONC y.com      Page 185 NOTE--By the marriage ofWilliam, 2nd Earl Warren an
2 CONC d the CountessIsabel, every known Europeanline and also those of the Fa
2 CONC r East fromearliest history were united.Isabel was twice married; first t
2 CONC o Robert de Bellomont, EarlofLiecester, and then to     William, 2nd Ea
2 CONC rl Warren as shownabove.Among the American families which descend from o
2 CONC ne or other ofthesemarriages are those of Washington, Lincoln, Grant, R
2 CONC oosevelt,Lee,Dewey, Scott, Emerson, Lowell, Dwight, Treat, Wolcott, Bac
2 CONC on,Ballou,Dimock, Sewall, Leavitt, Bulkeley, Cheney, Maxwell, Peck,Edwa
2 CONC rds,Huntington, Field, Ellsworth--and many others, for mention ofwhicht
2 CONC his space is too limited. All of the above are eligible tomembership in T
2 CONC he Order of the FirstCrusade by right of descent fromHugh the Great, on
2 CONC e of the sevengreat leaders who carried the Cross toJerusalem in 1096. O
2 CONC f the Barons of Runnymede (1215), the descendants ofat least a dozenare s
2 CONC imilarly     eligible; also many who trace to theearly KnightsGarter, o
2 CONC r to certain of the 'Mayflower' passengers. In theScotch line practical
2 CONC ly all Campbells in America are descendedfromHenry, 1st Earl Huntington (
2 CONC 8th from Malcolm I), who married AdaWarren,daughter of the 3rd Earl War
2 CONC ren. The greatest of all heritage is theknowledge that, however,lamenta
2 CONC ble be our own failure to attain thedesired results in life,there are b
2 CONC ehind us those who by sacrifice,suffering and undauntedcourage have not o
2 CONC nly left their mark on theworld of medieval times,but the memory of who
2 CONC se deeds will stand forthas a beacon-light solong as the Christian reli
2 CONC gion shall endure. Thoughwe cannot attain their heights, yet may we emu
2 CONC late theirexample and keepfresh their memory.
