1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Malcolm was born about 954. Malcolm's father Kenneth II, king of Scots,
2 CONC who died in 995, may have designated him as heir, but Malcolm becamekin
2 CONC g in 1005 only after the killing of his cousin Kenneth III. Hisreputati
2 CONC on rests on his extension of his kingdom's frontiers south tothe Tweed-
2 CONC Solway line. Though repulsed in 1006 at Durham, he defeated aNorthumbri
2 CONC an army at Carham in 1018 and asserted his claim to Lothian.In the west h
2 CONC e had the alliance of Strathclyde and, when its last kingdied, Malcolm s
2 CONC ecured the succession of his grandson, Duncan. Themarriage of his daugh
2 CONC ter to Sigurd the Stout, Norse Earl of Orkney, tookhis influence even f
2 CONC urther to the far north.
2 CONT
2 CONT Malcolm died at Glamis on 25 November 1034.
