1 NOTE Founder of Scotlands Dynasty. Whether Celtic or Norse in origin, thepag
2 CONC an kings of Scotland were considered to be sacred beings. At hisinaugur
2 CONC ation each king had to go through various religious rituals, as aresult o
2 CONC f which he and his people felt that the Lucky Spirit of thecommunity en
2 CONC tered and dwelt in the king's body, hence the belief thatthe royal fami
2 CONC lies descended from the gods. Since this Lucky Spirit'shuman manifestat
2 CONC ion could not be allowed to decay, such kings wereperiodically sacrific
2 CONC ed or slain by their rightful successors. Alpin,son of Eochaid IV 'the P
2 CONC oisonous', king of Dalriada, became king ofKintyre in March 834, only t
2 CONC o be killed in battle with the Picts inGalloway in August the same year
2 CONC .
