2 CONC heRomans against the Visigoths and the Saxons of the Loire. Although ap
2 CONC agan, he co-operated with the Gallic Church and laid the foundations of
2 CONC the kingdom which his descendants were to rule for the following threec
2 CONC enturies. The discovery of his grave in Tournai in 1653 revealed someas
2 CONC pects of his power: several hundred gold coins minted inConstantinople, s
2 CONC ent perhaps as a subsidy, and a gold brooch like thoseworn by Roman gen
2 CONC erals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Profession : Roi des Francs Saliens de 457 à 481.
