1 NOTE Hroðgar, Hrothgar, Hróarr, Hroar, Roar, Roas or Ro was a legendary Dani
2 CONC shking, living in the early 6th century.
2 CONT A Danish king Hroðgar appears in the Anglo-Saxon epics Beowulf andWidsi
2 CONC th, and also in Norse sagas, Norse poems, and medieval Danishchronicles
2 CONC . In both Anglo-Saxon and Scandinavian tradition, Hroðgar is aScylding, t
2 CONC he son of Healfdene, the brother of Halga, and the uncle ofHroðulf. Mor
2 CONC eover, in both traditions, the mentioned characters were thecontemporar
2 CONC ies of the Swedish king Eadgils; and both traditions alsomention a feud w
2 CONC ith men named Froda and Ingeld. The consensus view isthat Anglo-Saxon a
2 CONC nd Scandinavian traditions describe the same person
