1 NOTE When Bardanes Turcus and Nicephorus I were fighting over the Byzantinet
2 CONC hrone in 803, Leo at first joined Bardanes but later sided withNicephor
2 CONC us. Leo distinguished himself as a general under Nicephorus Iand Michae
2 CONC l I and became 'strategus' (general) of the Anatolikondistrict of the e
2 CONC mpire. He took part in the campaign of 813 against theBulgars but, when M
2 CONC ichael unwisely refused the peace terms they offered,the Asian troops u
2 CONC nder Leo deserted at the Battle of Versinkia, nearAdrianople. Leo then d
2 CONC eposed Michael I and, in July 813, replaced him.Meanwhile, Krum, the Bu
2 CONC lgarian Khan, had reached the walls ofConstantinople. Leo succeeded in d
2 CONC rawing him back and concluded a treatywith Krum's successor, Omortag, t
2 CONC hat determined the boundary between thetwo countries and provided a 30-
2 CONC year peace. In March 815 Leo deposed theOrthodox patriarch Nicephorus a
2 CONC nd convoked a synod for the followingmonth that reimposed the decrees o
2 CONC f the Iconoclast synod of Hieria of754, which had opposed the use of ic
2 CONC ons (religious images). Leo wasassasinated during a Christmas service i
2 CONC n the church of Hagia Sophia byfriends of Michael the Amorian, whom Leo h
2 CONC ad condemned to death the daybefore on a charge of treason. After the m
2 CONC urder Michael ascended thethrone as Michael II.
