1 NOTE Possible. La filiation avec sa mère reste à vérifier : Stuart le faitfi
2 CONC ls de Berthilde. Profession : Roi d'Austrasie de 634 à 656.
2 CONT
2 CONT FROM: Encyclopedia Britannica, www.britannica.com, Internet. SigebertII
2 CONC I (b. 630/631--d. Feb. 1, 656, Metz, Fr.), one of the first so-calledro
2 CONC is faineants ('sluggard kings') of the Merovingian dynasty, who heldno r
2 CONC eal power of his own but was ruled by whoever was his mayor of thepalac
2 CONC e.Made king of Austrasia by his father, Dagobert I, in 634,Sigebert was g
2 CONC overned first by Bishop Chunibert of Cologne and DukeAdalgisile; then, o
2 CONC n Dagobert's death, by Chunibert and Pepin I, themayor of the palace (d
2 CONC . 640); and finally by Pepin's son, Grimoald,mayor of the palace from 6
2 CONC 42 or 643 until the king's death.In the early640s, when a certain Otto w
2 CONC as mayor of the palace, Thuringia succeededin gaining effective autonom
2 CONC y at Austrasian expense. After Sigebert'sdeath, his young son, Dagobert I
2 CONC I, was sent off to an Irish monastery byGrimoald, who briefly establish
2 CONC ed his own son, Childebert (adopted bySigebert when the king was still c
2 CONC hildless) on the throne.
