1 NOTE From Encyclopedia Britannica Online, article titled 'Ferdinand III:''ca
2 CONC nonized Feb. 4, 1671; feast day May 30' 'also called SAINT FERDINAND,Sp
2 CONC anish SAN FERNANDO, king of Castilefrom 1217 to 1252 and of Leon from12
2 CONC 30 to 1252 and conqueror of theMuslim cities of Câordoba (1236), Jaâen(
2 CONC 1246), and Seville (1248).During his campaigns, Murcia submitted to his
2 CONC son Alfonso (laterAlfonso X), and the Muslim kingdom of Granada becameh
2 CONC is vassal. 'Ferdinand was the son of Alfonso IX of Leon and Berenguela,
2 CONC daughterof Alfonso VIII of Castile. When born, he was the heir to Leon,
2 CONC buthis uncle, Henry I of Castile, died young, and his motherinheritedth
2 CONC e crown of Castile, which she conferred on him. His father,likemany Leo
2 CONC nese, opposed the union, and Ferdinand found himself atwarwith him. By h
2 CONC is will Alfonso IX tried to disinherit his son, butthewill was set asid
2 CONC e, and Castile and Leon were permanently unitedin1230. 'Ferdinand marri
2 CONC ed Beatrice of Swabia, daughter of the HolyRomanemperor, a title that F
2 CONC erdinand's son Alfonso X was to claim.Hisconquest of Lower Andalusia wa
2 CONC s the result of the disintegrationofthe Almohad state. The Castilians a
2 CONC nd other conquerors occupiedthecities, driving out the Muslims and taki
2 CONC ng over vast estates.'
