1 NOTE Humphrey was Steward and Sewer to King Henry I. This feudal lordmarried
2 CONC Margery, daughter of Milo de Gloucester, Earl of Hereford,Lord HighCons
2 CONC table of England, last Lord Hereford of that family. Shewas co-heirwith h
2 CONC er sister Mabel. At the instigation of which Milo heespoused thecause o
2 CONC f the Empress Maud and her son, afterwards HenryII, against theKing Ste
2 CONC phen, and so faithfully maintained hisallegiance that theEmpress, by he
2 CONC r especial charter, granted him theoffice of steward andsewer, both in N
2 CONC ormandy and England. In the 20thof Henry II thisHumphrey accompanied Ri
2 CONC chard de Lacy, Justice ofEngland, into Scotlandwith a powerful army to w
2 CONC aste that country, andwas one of the witnessesto the accord made by Wil
2 CONC liam, King of Scots,and King Henry as to thesubjection of that kingdom t
2 CONC o the crown ofEngland. Humphrey, third Baronde Bohon (1109-87) succeede
2 CONC d his father Humphreythe great in 1129 andbecame involved in the strugg
2 CONC le for the throneof England on the death ofHenry I in 1134. When King H
2 CONC enry II becameking, Sir Humphrey becameSteward of Henry II's household a
2 CONC nd waslater named hereditary Constableof England, a position previously
2 CONC held by his father-in-law and then byhis brother-in-law. Humphrey, in11
2 CONC 38, had married Margaret, daughter ofMiles of Gloucester, Earl ofHerefo
2 CONC rd and High Constable of England. WhenMiles sons died heirless,Henry II g
2 CONC ave the title of High Constable toMiles' son-in-law,Humphrey, 3rd Baron d
2 CONC e Bohon. Humphrey and Margaret ofGloucester hadfive sons, Humphrey, Ric
2 CONC hard, John, Miles and Robert. KingHenry II (1154-89) had many difficult
2 CONC ies during his reign,includingnumerous revolts led by his sons. Humphre
2 CONC y (1109-87) thethird Baron deBohon, and his eldest son, Sir Humphrey (1
2 CONC 141-83)usually known as theYoung Earl of Hereford, remained loyal to He
2 CONC nryII throughout his reign.Sir John de Bohon, the third son, was a very
2 CONC close friend and supporterof Henry II's 4th son Geoffrey as long asGeof
2 CONC frey lived. Sir Robert deBohon, the youngest son, was a veryclose frien
2 CONC d of Prince Henry; HenryII's second son and heir. Sir Robert le Bon die
2 CONC d in 1183, four yearsbefore his father BaronHumphrey de Bohon's death. C
2 CONC onsequently, whenHumphrey the third Barondied in 1187, he was succeeded b
2 CONC y his 12 yearold grandson, Henry(1176-1220) as fourth Baron de Bohon. U
2 CONC pon coming ofage, Henry wasknighted and made High Constable of England a
2 CONC nd held manorhouses andcastles at Caldicot, Haresfield, Oaksey and Wald
2 CONC en in additionto themain Hereford holdings.
