1 NOTE He was named First Earl of Pembroke in 1138; became a baron by obtainin
2 CONC gthe estates of his paternal uncles Roger and Walter, both of whom died
2 CONC without offspring.  When he was named Earl of Pembroke, King Stephenals
2 CONC o gave him the rape and castle of Pevensy.  When the Empress landedin 1
2 CONC 139, Gilbert marched with the King to Arundel.  At the battle ofLincoln
2 CONC , Feb. 2, 1140/41, he was one of those nobles who fled when thefirst di
2 CONC vision of Stephen's army was put to flight, but then reallied tothe Que
2 CONC en after she recovered London in June.  He waswith Stephen at thesiege o
2 CONC f Oxford in 1142 and, in 1144, invaded South Wales and capturedor built (
2 CONC differing versions from differentsources) Carmarthen Castle.He was a be
2 CONC nefactor to the abbey ofTintern and the priories of Lewes ,Southward an
2 CONC d St. Neots, and theTemplars. (Complete Peerage, VolX:348-350)
