2 CONC obtained from Henry II the whole county of Meath. He wassubsequentlycon
2 CONC stituted Governor of Dublin, and Justice of Ireland.But incurring thedi
2 CONC spleasure of his royal master by marrying, withoutlicense, thedaughter o
2 CONC f the King of Connaught, he was divested, in1181, of thecustody of the m
2 CONC etropolis of Dublin. In four years he wasmurdered by oneMalvo Miadaich, i
2 CONC n revenge for the severity with whichhe had treated theworkmen employed b
2 CONC y him in erecting the Castle ofLurhedy. He left issueWalter, his succes
2 CONC sor, Hugh, Constable ofIreland, and a daughter,Elayne.
