1 NOTE He was known as 'Black Will', he was the 6th Baron of Braiose,Descenden
2 CONC tof Griffith, Prince of Wales. William de Braose fell victim to thejeal
2 CONC ousy of Llewellyn, Prince ofWales, who suspecting an intimacybetween hi
2 CONC m and the princess, hiswife, King Henry's sister, invited himto an East
2 CONC er feast, andtreacherously cast him in prison at theconclusion of the b
2 CONC anquet. Hewas soon afterwards put to death with theunfortunate princess
2 CONC . He hadmarried Eve (Eva) Marshal, daughter ofWilliam Marshal, and sist
2 CONC er ofRichard, Earl of Pembroke, by whom he hadfour daughters, hisco-hei
2 CONC rs. He was the Earl of Abergavenny. Lord ofAbergavenny.Sixth Baron deBr
2 CONC aiose.  He was hanged by Llewelyn Fawr in1230. From DougThompson;http:/
2 CONC /freespace.virgin.net/doug.thompson/BraoseWeb/index1.htm:'William succe
2 CONC eded his father as Lord of Abergavenny, Builth andotherMarcher Lordship
2 CONC s in 1227.  Styled by the Welsh as 'Black William'hewas imprisoned by L
2 CONC lewelyn ap Iorwerth in 1229 during Hubert deBurgh'sdisastrous Kerry (Ce
2 CONC ri) campaign. He was ransomed and releasedafter ashort captivity during w
2 CONC hich he agreed to cede Builth as amarriageportion for his daughter Isab
2 CONC ella on her etrothal to David,son and heirof Llewelyn. The following Ea
2 CONC ster, Llewelyn discovered anintriguebetween his wife, Joan, and William
2 CONC .  Supported by a generalclamour forhis death, Llewelyn had William pub
2 CONC licly hanged on 2nd May1230.'
