1 NOTE This nobleman rebelled against King Henry II and, marching at thehead o
2 CONC fthe Leicestershire men upon Nottingham, then kept for the KingbyRegina
2 CONC ld de Lucie, got possession of the town, which he sacked,puttingthe gre
2 CONC ater part of the inhabitants to the sword and takingthe restprisoners. H
2 CONC e soon afterwards, however was reduced tosubmission andobliged to surre
2 CONC nder to the crown his castles ofTutbury and Duffield,which were demolis
2 CONC hed by order of the king. Hislordship married Sibilla,daughter of Willi
2 CONC am de Braose, Lord ofAbergavenny and Brecknock, by whomhe had issue: Wi
2 CONC lliam, hissuccessor; Milicent married Roger Mortimer ofWigmore; Agatha,
2 CONC concubine to King John, by whom she had Jaone, whomarried Llewellynthe G
2 CONC reat, Prince of North Wales; Anghared marriedLlewelly Vychan,grandson o
2 CONC f Lord Rhys, Prince of South Wales. He was theEarl Of Derby.
