2 NOTE Richard Lionheart is king of England after Henry's Death London, 3Septe
3 CONC mber 1189 Richard Lionheart, crowned king of England today, knowslittle o
3 CONC f thecountry he has inherited. He has spent most of his life inFrance, a
3 CONC sduke of Aquitaine ruling the land of his mother, Eleanor, andfightingh
3 CONC is father, Henry 11, and his brothers. The old king's dyingwords tohis p
3 CONC ugnacious, disloyal son were: 'God grant that I may not dietill I have h
3 CONC ad a fitting revenge onyou.' Richard, aged 32, grew up inan atmosphere o
3 CONC f intrigue. Henry hadacquired vast territories in Franceby his marriage
3 CONC , and his sons werenever satisfied with their shares.When Richard's eld
3 CONC er brother Henrydied and he became heir, his fatherwanted him to leave A
3 CONC quitaine andcome to England.  Richard scornfullyrefused and another fam
3 CONC ily war,the last in fact, ensued. Richard's firstact as king was to rel
3 CONC ease his mother, who had beenconfined atWinchester for supporting him a
3 CONC gainst her husband. He hasbeen busyraising money for an expedition to P
3 CONC alestine. He can hardlywait to beoff crusading once more. The nick name '
3 CONC Lionheart' wasgiven to him inFrance, as coeur de lion, for his military p
3 CONC rowess.
