2 CONC ICHARD HAD THE CHRIST CHURCH CATHEDRAL IN DUBLIN REBUILT IN STONEAFTER1
2 CONC 169 FOR THE LAURENCE O'TOOLE, ARCHBISHOP OF DUBLIN.  THERE IS AMEMORIAL
2 CONC IN THE CATHEDRAL NAVE FOR RICHARD SOURCE--ANCESTRAL ROOTS OF CERTAINAME
2 CONC RICAN COLONISTS WHO CAME TOAMERICA BEFORE 1700, SEVENTH EDITION,COPYRIG
2 CONC HT 1995, PAGE 69 FromEncyclopedia Britannica Online, articletitled 'Pem
2 CONC broke, RichardFitzGilbert, 2nd Earl of:' 'byname RICHARDSTRONGBOW, also c
2 CONC alled RICHARD DE CLARE, Anglo-Normanlord whose invasionof Ireland in 11
2 CONC 70 initiated the opening phase ofthe English conquest.'The son of Gilbe
2 CONC rt de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke, he succeeded tohisfather's estates i
2 CONC n southern Wales in 1148/49. Pembroke hadevidentlylost these lands by 1
2 CONC 168; it was probably in that year thathe agreed toaid Dermot MacMurroug
2 CONC h, king of Leinster, who had beenexpelled from hiskingdom by Roderic (R
2 CONC ory O'Connor), high king ofIreland. King Henry IIof England (reigned 11
2 CONC 54-89) granted Pembrokepermission to invadeIreland, and on Aug. 23, 117
2 CONC 0, the earl landednear Waterford. Waterfordand Dublin quickly fell to t
2 CONC he Normans. After the death ofMacMurrough inMay 1171, Pembroke was besi
2 CONC eged in Dublin by Roderic,but in Septemberhis forces broke out and rout
2 CONC ed Roderic's army. Inorder to preventPembroke from setting himself up a
2 CONC s an independentruler, Henry II hadhim acknowledge royal authority over h
2 CONC is conquestsin Leinster. Pembrokehelped the king suppress a rebellion i
2 CONC n Normandyin 1173-74, and inreturn Henry granted him custody of Wexford
2 CONC ,Waterford, and Dublin. Bythe time Pembroke died, all Ireland had beenc
2 CONC ommitted to his care, butwithin Ireland his supremacy was recognizedonl
2 CONC y in Leinster. 'His sonGilbert de Striguil (or Strigoil) died unmarried
2 CONC , certainlybefore 1189,and as a minor was never styled earl. The earldo
2 CONC m passedwith Richard'sdaughter Isabel (d. 1220) to her husband WilliamM
2 CONC arshal, the 1st Earl ofPembroke in the Marshal line.'
