1 NOTE From Encyclopedia Britannica Online, article titled 'Alfonso VIII:''byn
2 CONC ame EL DE LAS NAVAS (SPANISH: HE OF LAS NAVAS), king of Castilefrom1158
2 CONC , son of Sancho III, whom he succeeded when three years old. 'BeforeAlf
2 CONC onso came of age his reign was troubled by internal strifeand theinterv
2 CONC ention of the kingdom of Navarre in Castilian affairs.Throughouthis rei
2 CONC gn he maintained a close alliance with the kingdomof Aragon, andin 1179 h
2 CONC e concluded the Pact of Cazorla, which settledthe future lineof demarca
2 CONC tion between Castile and Aragon when thereconquest of MoorishSpain was c
2 CONC ompleted. From 1172 to 1212 he wasengaged in resistance tothe Moorish A
2 CONC lmohad invaders, who defeatedhim in 1195. In the same yearthe kings of L
2 CONC eon and Navarre invadedCastile, but Alfonso defeated themwith the aid o
2 CONC f King Peter II ofAragon. In 1212 Alfonso secured a greatvictory at Las N
2 CONC avas de Tolosaover the Almohad sultan and thereby brokeAlmohad power in S
2 CONC pain.'
