1 NOTE From Encyclopedia Britannica Online, article titled 'Alfonso I:' 'alsoc
2 CONC alled Afonso Henriques, byname AFONSO THE CONQUEROR, PortugueseAFONSO O
2 CONC CONQUISTADOR, the first king of Portugal (1139-85), whoconqueredSantarâ
2 CONC em and Lisbon from the Muslims (1147) and securedPortugueseindependence f
2 CONC rom Leon (1139). 'Alfonso VI, emperor of Leon,had granted the county of P
2 CONC ortugal toAfonso's father, Henry of Burgundy,who successfully defended i
2 CONC tagainst the Muslims (1095-1112). Henrymarried Alfonso VI'sillegitimate d
2 CONC aughter, Teresa, who governed Portugalfrom the time ofher husband's dea
2 CONC th (1112) until her son Afonso came ofage. Sherefused to cede her power t
2 CONC o Afonso, but his party prevailed intheBattle of Säao Mamede, near Guim
2 CONC aräaes (1128). Though at firstobligedas a vassal to submit to his cousi
2 CONC n Alfonso VII of Leon,Afonsoassumed the title of king in 1139. 'By vict
2 CONC ory in the Battle ofOurique (1139) he was able to imposetribute on his M
2 CONC uslim neighbours;and in 1147 he further capturedSantarâem and, availing h
2 CONC imself of theservices of passing crusaders,successfully laid siege to L
2 CONC isbon. Hecarried his frontiers beyond theTagus River, annexing Beja in 1
2 CONC 162 andâEvora in 1165; in attackingBadajoz, he was taken prisoner but t
2 CONC henreleased. He married Mafaldaof Savoy and associated his son, Sancho I
2 CONC ,with his power. By the timeof his death he had created a stable andind
2 CONC ependent monarchy.'
