2 CONC trongholds and castles. Tofacilitate his plans, he encouragedforeign se
2 CONC ttlers and enlistedbishops, religious orders, and nobles inhis coloniza
2 CONC tion projects,granting vast territories to the militaryorders (the Hosp
2 CONC italers, the Templars, the Orders ofCalatrava andSantiago).  After an i
