2 TYPE Misc
2 NOTE was the first Crispo to settle in Havre Boucher. According to Edme Rame
3 CONC aude Saint-Pere, a french historian who visited Havre Boucher in the186
3 CONC 0s, noted that the name Crispo is of Portugese origin.
3 CONT Family tradition has passed down the story that two Crispo brothers, on
3 CONC ebeing Marc, deserted ship in Havre Boucher. They were hidden in the ho
3 CONC meof a Webb family until the departure of the ship. Marc eventuallymarr
3 CONC ied Marguerite Webb. His brother is said to have moved on toCalifornia.
