1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT The family of Bullen (Boleyne or Boleyn) is said to have been of ancien
2 CONC tdate in the county of Norfolk. Geoffrey Boleyn came from Salle, County
2 CONC Norfolk, but settled in London. In 1429 Geoffrey Boleyn was admitted to
2 CONC The Mercer's Company by redemption (i.e. by invitation, as opposed to b
2 CONC yapprenticeship or by patrimony). He attained great opulence but alsofi
2 CONC lled the lord mayor's chair and was made a knight. He married theeldest d
2 CONC aughter and co-heir of Lord Hoo and Hastings and they hadseveral childr
2 CONC en.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1475 the Register of the Fraternity of the Holy Trinity at Luton,whi
2 CONC ch had been founded that year, mentions Thomas Hoo, Lord Hastings,and E
2 CONC lizabeth his wife; Sir Geoffrey Boleyn, late Lord Mayor of London,and D
2 CONC ame Anne, his wife, daughter of the said Lord Hastings; WilliamBoleyn, e
2 CONC squire; Thomas Hoo, esquire; Thomas Hoo of Walden; and LaurenceHoo of E
2 CONC ast Hyde and Alice, his wife.
